# result — a confirmed write reports its outcome through a renderer that
# honours --json (INVARIANTS.md H-10, applied to the branch that WROTE).
#
# This is a VIOLATION surface, the mirror image of preview.manifest:
# internal/surfaceaudit.ResultSurface lists only the --confirm-gated
# entrypoints that print their result straight to the caller's stdout with no
# --json branch above the line. Empty is the goal. The extractor is guarded
# against silently matching nothing by TestResultExtractorFlagsProseOnConfirm,
# which feeds it a known-bad function, rather than by a non-empty check.
#
# It was not empty. Fifty-three lines across twenty entrypoints were prose under
# --json on the SUCCESS path of a write — `svc call --confirm --json` printed
# `called script.turn_on` immediately after really firing the script, exit 0,
# and area/label/floor create+delete, tpl create+delete, script/auto/helper
# create+delete+apply, dash create+save+delete+replace, ent set-area/set-label,
# device set-area/set-label, config delete and rollback all did the same. The
# preview half of the identical law was closed one release earlier, by a fix
# whose scope was the word "preview".
#ceiling 0
